'''Cockatrice''' are [[Slayer monsters]] that require level 25 [[Slayer]] to kill. A [[mirror shield]] or [[V's shield]] is ''highly'' recommended. Without one, the cockatrice will attack with its piercing gaze, which has a range of 5 tiles, hits for 11 damage that can be negated by Protect from Melee, and rapidly drains combat stats. Otherwise, do not expect much of a fight from cockatrices. As 20 [[Defence]] is needed to wield a mirror shield, players who do not meet this requirement will not be assigned them as a task.

They are rarely killed outside of Slayer tasks, generally only by those hunting the rare [[mystic boots (light)]] and [[cockatrice head]] drops.

If necessary, players can utilise the large rock formation to the north of the cave to safespot cockatrice on the opposite side, even without a mirror shield, due to the limited range of piercing gaze. This is useful for pures who cannot wield a mirror shield, or for players who wish to use two-handed weapons like shortbows, but it is not generally recommended. Note that cockatrice have a unique mechanic where they will "retaliate" against any player who is within 10 tiles and is attempting to attack them without a mirror shield, even if the player has not actually attacked yet. This can be exploited to aggro distant cockatrice by merely red-clicking them.

A [[dwarf multicannon]] cannot be set up in the Fremmenik Slayer Caves. Those looking to use a cannon should kill [[moonlight cockatrice]] instead (requires 48 Slayer to begin the [[Perilous Moons]] quest. For access to [[Neypotzli]], only partial completion of the [[Perilous Moons]] quest is required).

